# stabbur has no project-local configuration values.
#
# monorepo-merge config layering invariant: a value used by more than one
# project lives in the repository root `.env`; a value used by exactly one
# project lives in that project's `.env`; no value appears in two files.
# Everything stabbur needs is either shared or derived:
#
#   STABBUR_POSTGRES_PASSWORD -> root .env (one key PER database, not one
#                            shared value — see D151 and design.md: Postgres
#                            only applies a password to a FRESH data dir)
#   INTERNAL_TOKEN        -> root .env   (every service-to-service leg;
#                            unified-auth 4.6 collapsed STABBUR_AUTH_TOKEN
#                            and SMIA_AUTH_TOKEN into this one value)
#   DATABASE_URL          -> derived in stabbur/compose.yaml from
#                            STABBUR_POSTGRES_PASSWORD; never typed
#   SMIA_BASE_URL         -> derived from smia's service name
#                            (http://smia-backend:5055); never typed
#
# So: do not create stabbur/.env. Copy the root .env.example to the root
# .env instead. This file exists only to say that, and should be deleted
# the moment stabbur gains a value that genuinely belongs to it alone.
#
# Not configuration, but file-shaped and easy to confuse with it:
# stabbur/cookies.txt (YTDLP_COOKIES_FILE, manual-link-audio-capture) is a
# gitignored YouTube session export, bind-mounted read-only by
# stabbur/compose.yaml. See the comment there.
